    "body": "Docs only. Three files under `nix/sandhi/docs/`. No runtime, workflow or protocol changes.\n\n- **DECISIONS.md (new 2026-10-05 entry).** Records F5 as deferred, quoting Tessera's trigger and fault model from [turn 2](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/1#issuecomment-5963017053), as Sideband promised in [turn 3](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/1#issuecomment-5963414463). Also records Mora's lead assignments, quoted from [5963129962](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/1#issuecomment-5963129962). Cites archived body records on `anchor-archive`. The 2026-10-02 entry is unchanged. This covers the \"attributed DECISIONS.md entry\" that PR #4's handoff says is still needed.\n- **SIDEBAND.md.** The standing prompt for a new session, the receiver's details and Sideband's open commitments. It also documents an observed issue: the receiver has held an unposted turn-5 draft since 2026-10-03, waiting for Mora's direct go-ahead in its session.\n- **NAME-RESOLUTION.md.** A design note for DNS as a declared mechanism. It covers a declared name → single resolver unit → epoch-bound, expiring publication → start gate, with `runtimeMaxSec` bounding staleness. It compares two enforcement options and keeps \"address authorization is not identity\" explicit. It also corrects Sideband's turn-3 claim that runtime resolution failures belong in a Lopa snapshot. It proposes one experiment to run now: can a contract already resolve names through a host Unix socket? All systemd and nftables behaviour is marked as untested hypotheses.\n\nThis does not touch `HANDOFF.md`, so it does not conflict with #4.\n\nValidation: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passed (15 tests). `python3 anchor.py verify` verified 10 records. The Sandhi workflow is path-filtered and excludes `docs/`, so it will not run.\n\nContext read: AGENTS.md, PROTOCOL.md, HANDOFF.md and DECISIONS.md at `ff75d2a`; PR #1 comments through 5963429159; PR #4 at `7f9e762`; `modules/vidhi.nix`, README and the Lopa v2 schema at `ff75d2a`; the receiver routine's configuration and transcript. There is no archived context manifest, so this is a declared gap. Merging is Mora's decision.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015f2oo3zcddjSg7k3FsoRgS\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_015f2oo3zcddjSg7k3FsoRgS)_",
